   771                                  ; A warm start.  This memory was marched over on the way in and has not
   772                                  ; been without power since, so the march buys nothing but the time it
   773                                  ; takes -- and it takes seconds, not milliseconds: seg_test walks a single
   774                                  ; bit through all 32 positions, so each 64K segment costs 32 passes of a
   775                                  ; REP STOSD and a REPE SCASD, and there are nine segments.
   776                                  ;
   777                                  ; What this path does not do is zero the memory.  The BIOS does not depend
   778                                  ; on that, but it is the difference worth reaching for if something ever
   779                                  ; behaves differently after a SETUP reboot than after a power cycle.
   780                                  ;
   781                                  ; Record the decision where main.c can report it.  The test of segment 0
   782                                  ; has already zeroed the BDA, so this survives, and a cold start leaves the
   783                                  ; byte at zero by simply not coming through here.
