   808                                  %if SHADOW_MODE
   809                                  ;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;
   810                                  ; Shadow the ROM into DRAM
   811                                  ;
   812                                  ; The BIOS executes from 8-bit ROM at 5 wait states, and every INT 10h
   813                                  ; character and every IDE sector pays for it.  CS2 already covers the whole
   814                                  ; first megabyte of DRAM -- 16 bits wide at 2 wait states -- and the two
   815                                  ; overlap at F0000.  While UCS is enabled it is the one that answers there,
   816                                  ; so the ROM cannot simply be copied over itself: the copy has to run from
   817                                  ; somewhere else while UCS is switched off.
   818                                  ;
   819                                  ;   1. copy the ROM to a scratch segment, and check it arrived
   820                                  ;   2. jump into that copy, so execution is no longer inside the ROM
   821                                  ;   3. switch UCS off -- F0000 answers from DRAM from here on
   822                                  ;   4. copy the scratch back to F0000, and check it arrived
   823                                  ;   5. jump back to F000, which is now the DRAM copy
   824                                  ;
   825                                  ; Either check can fail without consequence.  A failure at step 1 leaves the
   826                                  ; ROM exactly as it was; a failure at step 4 switches UCS back on and returns
   827                                  ; to the real ROM.  Slower, but running.  Neither is expected -- but the DRAM
   828                                  ; under F0000 is the one part of the first megabyte that test_1to8 does not
   829                                  ; reach, and this is what writes to it, so it gets checked here instead.
   830                                  ;
   831                                  ; Between step 3 and the end of step 4, nothing may read DGROUP data or call
   832                                  ; anything that does: DS-relative reads land at F0000, which is uninitialised
   833                                  ; DRAM until that copy finishes.  That is why this stretch is bare string
   834                                  ; moves and port writes, with DS pointed at the scratch and not at DGROUP.
   835                                  ;
   836                                  ; This is done here rather than earlier because it needs DRAM that has been
   837                                  ; tested, and it must be before anything records a F000-relative address.
   838                                  ;
   839                                  ; One consequence worth knowing: F0000 is writable afterwards.  Writes into
   840                                  ; the BIOS used to fall on ROM and do nothing; now they land.  Nothing in
   841                                  ; this BIOS writes there -- _DATA and _BSS are empty by design -- but a stray
   842                                  ; far pointer that used to be harmless is not any more.
   843                                  ;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;;
   844                                  SHADOW_SEG	equ	XFER_AD>>4	; scratch, inside the range just tested
   845                                  SHADOW_WORDS	equ	32768		; 64K, as words
   846                                  
